 farmers will get a smaller crop  the message now from government is use  water wisely but water supply supplies  will remain resilient it's possible the  environment agency will separately apply  for drought orders but ultimately it's  up to water companies to put in place  their agreed uh drought plans they are  in charge of hosepipe bans and just to  recap parts of the southwest the  southern central england and east of  england have moved cymer into drought  status the public being told to use  their water wisely but water supplies  for now remain resilient
 

